Owner ruling 2026-10-25 (option A, project frame) on the 2026-07-15
supply_chain_tier concept audit's F1. ADR-0041 §1 said tier is "the
supply-chain distance of code from the project under analysis" but named
neither the project's extent nor what a declaration or a boundary stub
measures, and its row 2 put monorepo siblings in tier 2 -- so a sibling was
tier 1 as its own package node and tier 2 / 3 as a declaration. INV-kutub
(PR #1890) made the code agree with the ruling; this is the document half.
Rewritten in place, no addendum or history (docs/adr/README.md lifecycle).

ADR-0041:
* §1 axiom: tier names the supply-chain distance, from the project under
  analysis, of the code a node stands for -- the project being every
  package whose source is in the analysed tree; where the node is written,
  how the code is declared and what produced the node may not influence
  it. A file / function / project / package node stands for its own code,
  a dependency declaration for the package it names, a boundary stub for
  the code it replaces; nodes standing for one package carry one tier;
  tiers 1-3 are distances, tier 4 the derived-artifact exception.
* Row 1 includes workspace siblings; row 2 is org-internal code outside
  the project (internal_package_roots), with no CLI path supplying it, so
  a CLI run emits no tier-2 node.
* Cut the "irony recorded for posterity" paragraph and the 2026-07-17
  WI-popok annotation (history), keeping §2's META-bifif rule; corrected
  §2's claim that directness is stamped on dependency nodes (only boundary
  nodes carry it -- INV-fuhin); replaced the stale prediction that tier 2
  "fills with the 7 workspace packages"; the tracker list's WI-popok row
  now says wont_do / not a re-derivation, and INV-kutub is listed.

Spec §14: "classifies files by their position in the dependency graph" ->
classifies nodes by distance; the axiom paragraph states the frame; the
"(History: ...)" paragraph is cut to current facts; the directness /
ecosystem sentence no longer claims declarations carry them (checked on
merged dev: no dependency node has meta.directness or meta.ecosystem); the
tier-2 row and section say no CLI path supplies internal_package_roots
(checked: .hypergumbo.toml with that key exits 2 "unknown setting") and
mark it 🟧 blocked on WI-jaloz's wire-or-delete decision, and the
capsule-plan YAML example (that plan was removed in 03223627a4) is gone.

